name walk_cliff
describe Goal 235's viewed check: walk straight into a face too steep to climb and stay at the bottom of it. The line from (0,16) along +X rises 25.9 -> 33.6 -> 39.9 -> 50.4 -> 61.9 m over sixteen metres -- measured with tools/svo_render --xz, and that is 57 to 71 degrees, well past the 40 degree walkable limit. Before the limit existed the body walked straight up it, because at 7.8 mm voxels every slope is a sub-centimetre staircase and a 4 cm step budget climbs any staircase. The capture is the body looking at the wall it is not going to climb.
backend both

option --walk
option --no-taa

pose_ground 0,16 -90 0 1.7
hold forward+boost 6
hold none 1
wait 2


# GOLDEN POLICY (measured, this scenario has none / only the early ones):
# A capture taken after sustained MOTION is not reproducible on this engine today. Two identical
# runs of the same scenario differ by 5.3% to 35.5% of pixels, because at speed the body outruns the
# LOD rebuild and which tree is resident when it stops decides what it sees. Captures taken AT REST
# reproduce to 0.0001-0.11%, well under the 1.5% gate. So the moving captures here are written for
# eyeballing and deliberately have no golden until Prompt 004 removes the rebuild storm.

capture end walk_cliff no-golden
assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6
assert walk_violations == 0
assert inside_solid == 0
